{"id": "the-veiled-utterance", "ids": "⿰口⿳冖罒⿱一又", "title": "The Veiled Utterance", "pronunciation": "wǎng", "bopomofo": "ㄨㄤˇ", "meaning": "To speak in riddles or speak while concealing one's true intent", "formation": "phono-semantic", "definitions": [{"zh": "以口言而覆其意，隱語也", "en": "To speak with the mouth while concealing one's meaning; cryptic speech"}, {"zh": "設網以誘，巧言令色", "en": "To set verbal traps through honeyed words and pleasing countenance"}, {"zh": "言辭曲折，不直其心", "en": "Circuitous speech that does not reveal one's true heart"}], "etymology": "In the lost dialects of court intrigue, there should have been a character for the peculiar art of speaking while wearing a veil of words. The mouth radical suggests speech, while the covering element (冖) draped over the net-like structure (罒) evokes the deliberate obscuring of meaning—as if one's words were caught in a web of intention, visible yet unreachable. This character would have captured what plain deception cannot: the melancholy beauty of necessary concealment.", "source": {"work": "《廣韻》", "gloss": "烏往切，音網。隱言也。"}, "components": [{"char": "口", "meaning": "mouth"}, {"char": "冖", "meaning": "cover"}, {"char": "罒", "meaning": "罒"}, {"char": "一", "meaning": "一"}, {"char": "又", "meaning": "又"}], "examples": [{"text": "君子不⿰口⿳冖罒⿱一又，小人多⿰口⿳冖罒⿱一又而欺世。", "translation": "The gentleman does not speak in riddles; the petty man often speaks cryptically to deceive the world.", "style": "classical"}, {"text": "她總是⿰口⿳冖罒⿱一又地回答，讓人摸不清真意。", "translation": "She always answers evasively, making it impossible for others to grasp her true meaning.", "style": "contemporary"}], "related": [{"char": "網", "pinyin": "wǎng", "gloss": "net, web"}, {"char": "謊", "pinyin": "huǎng", "gloss": "lie, falsehood"}, {"char": "隱", "pinyin": "yǐn", "gloss": "conceal, hide"}], "tags": ["deception", "speech", "concealment", "rhetoric"], "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\">\n<style>@import url(\